<figure class="qe-figure qe-flow" aria-labelledby="row-flow-title">
 <figcaption id="row-flow-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Three orders become two customer totals</figcaption>
 <div class="qe-stage">
  <ol class="qe-pipeline" aria-label="Operations in this hand trace">
   <li data-node="0">Read orders <small>3 rows examined</small></li>
   <li data-node="1">Keep October paid orders <small>2 orders emitted</small></li>
   <li data-node="2">Match their order lines <small>3 matching lines emitted</small></li>
   <li data-node="3">Add line values by customer <small>2 groups emitted</small></li>
   <li data-node="4">Sort by value, then ID <small>2 rows returned</small></li>
  </ol>
  <div class="qe-stream"><p class="qe-label" data-flow-label data-live>Stored orders</p><div data-flow-rows data-live></div></div>
 </div>
 <p class="qe-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="qe-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 1 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span></div>
 <div class="qe-hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <p class="qe-caption">A hand trace of one possible route, not an observed plan. Each arrow means that one operation supplies rows to the next. The drawing omits columns each later operation does not need.</p>
 <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><p>Orders 101 (Mina, paid), 102 (Tariq, paid), 103 (Mina, pending) are all in October. Filtering keeps 101 and 102. Their lines are 101/1 = 4.50, 101/2 = 35.00 and 102/1 = 40.00. Grouping gives customer 1 = 39.50 and customer 2 = 40.00. Sorting returns customer 2 first, then customer 1.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll('.qe-flow').forEach(root=>{
 const stages=[
 {label:'Stored orders',rows:[['101 · customer 1','12 Oct · paid'],['102 · customer 2','14 Oct · paid'],['103 · customer 1','20 Oct · pending']],text:'All three orders are in October. Reading a row is work even when a later test rejects it.'},
 {label:'Eligible orders · one row per order',rows:[['101 · customer 1','paid'],['102 · customer 2','paid']],text:'The date and status tests keep 101 and 102. Order 103 contributes nothing to this paid-order report.'},
 {label:'Matching lines · one row per line',rows:[['101 / 1 · customer 1','1 × 4.50 = 4.50'],['101 / 2 · customer 1','1 × 35.00 = 35.00'],['102 / 1 · customer 2','2 × 20.00 = 40.00']],text:'Matching on order ID gives three line rows. The two occurrences for order 101 are both needed.'},
 {label:'Groups · one row per customer',rows:[['Customer 1 · Mina','4.50 + 35.00 = 39.50'],['Customer 2 · Tariq','40.00 = 40.00']],text:'The aggregate consumes the line values and keeps a running total for each customer. Its output has two rows, but producing them required all three line values.'},
 {label:'Final result · requested order',rows:[['Customer 2 · Tariq','40.00'],['Customer 1 · Mina','39.50']],text:'Sorting puts 40.00 before 39.50. The first result cannot be chosen until the totals it must compare are complete.'}
 ];
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>stages.length,draw(n){const s=stages[n]; root.querySelector('[data-flow-label]').textContent=s.label;root.querySelector('[data-flow-rows]').replaceChildren(...s.rows.map(([key,val])=>{const row=document.createElement('p');const a=document.createElement('strong');a.textContent=key;const b=document.createElement('span');b.textContent=val;row.append(a,b);return row;}));root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=s.text;root.querySelectorAll('[data-node]').forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('qe-current',i===n));}});
 });
</script>
